Chapter: Vec4LanePastEnd
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The same refusal on the OTHER builtin, whose lane count is four rather
 than two. `vec-extract` and `vec4-extract` carry different vectors in
 their types, so a check that hardcoded one count would pass one of these
 two files and fail the other.

 Lane 4 is the first illegal lane of a `Vector 4`. The last LEGAL one,
 lane 3, is read by codex/test/vector-f32.codex, which is the positive
 control that this bound is not off by one in the refusing direction.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (from-real-approx (vec4-extract (vec4-splat (to-real-approx 1.5)) 4)))
  end

